{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Vor37Zu8jB51CfnizHgMin", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych\"}, {\"url\": \"https://uen.pressbooks.pub/arth2720/chapter/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-diptych/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://smarthistory.org/?p=1926\"}, {\"url\": \"https://guyhepner.com/news/andy-warhol-marilyn-series-collectors-guide\"}, {\"url\": \"https://WikiArt.org/en/andy-warhol/marilyn-diptych-1962\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hessen.museum-digital.de/pdf/object/128330.pdf?lang=de\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.phillips.com/zh/detail/andy-warhol/89851\"}, {\"url\": \"https://lbas.lboro.ac.uk/poster/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-poster.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://artlovers.travel/en/artworks/marilyn-diptych\"}, {\"url\": \"https://rachel.core2learn.org/modules/en-learnsaylor/mod/page/MarilynDiptychArt.pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:58:27.396Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Marilyn Diptych Warhol publicity photo Niagara 1953 Rose Loomis", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_013PK9Nd3Teu9ickM8x9mkAP", "content": [{"title": "Marilyn Diptych", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marilyn_Diptych"}, {"title": "Andy Warhol, Marilyn Monroe Diptych", "url": "https://uen.pressbooks.pub/arth2720/chapter/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-diptych/"}, {"title": "smarthistory.org", "url": "https://smarthistory.org/?p=1926"}, {"title": "andy warhol marilyn series collectors guide", "url": "https://guyhepner.com/news/andy-warhol-marilyn-series-collectors-guide"}, {"title": "marilyn diptych 1962", "url": "https://WikiArt.org/en/andy-warhol/marilyn-diptych-1962"}, {"title": "hessen.museum-digital.de", "url": "https://hessen.museum-digital.de/pdf/object/128330.pdf?lang=de"}, {"title": "www.phillips.com", "url": "https://www.phillips.com/zh/detail/andy-warhol/89851"}, {"title": "Andy Warhol Marilyn Monroe Poster", "url": "https://lbas.lboro.ac.uk/poster/andy-warhol-marilyn-monroe-poster.html"}, {"title": "Marilyn Diptych", "url": "https://artlovers.travel/en/artworks/marilyn-diptych"}, {"title": "rachel.core2learn.org", "url": "https://rachel.core2learn.org/modules/en-learnsaylor/mod/page/MarilynDiptychArt.pdf"}]}, "The search confirms the core facts. The Tate's 1962 Marilyn Diptych is built on a 1953 publicity still from *Niagara*, which Gene Kornman photographed. Warhol made it shortly after Monroe's death, and the still was the basis for much of his later Marilyn work.\n\n- **Source photo:** One account credits Gene Kornman with the still, and another says the film was Monroe's 1953 release for 20th Century Fox. The painting consists of fifty repeated images based on a publicity still from the 1953 film Niagara photographed by Gene Kornman.\n- **Character:** A German museum description identifies Monroe's role as the ruthless wife Rose Loomis, which matches the character name in your query.\n- **Timing:** The work was completed during the weeks after Marilyn Monroe's death in August 1962.\n- **Later works:** The same still became the basis for a large body of Marilyn works created between 1962 and 1967.\n- **Discrepancy:** Sources disagree on the holding institution. Wikipedia and WikiArt place the painting at the Tate, while a PDF on core2learn lists the National Gallery of Victoria. The Tate attribution is more consistent across sources, but I haven't verified it against the museum's own site."], "durationSeconds": 6.817426791999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Vor37Zu8jB51CfnizHgMin", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
